Theorem RL-2: Last-use RcDec emission

  Preconditions:
    - F is an ArcFunction per arc.md sec-Key-Types
    - AimsStateMap M is converged for F (per IA-7)
    - owned_non_scalar_vars(F) per Annex E §AIMS RL-2
    - uses(v) is the set of program points where v is used in F
    - last_use(v) = max_program_point(uses(v))
    - Ownership-transferring last uses per RL-2:
        Return, Construct/Reuse/CollectionReuse arg, Set value,
        PartialApply capture, Apply/Invoke to Owned param,
        Jump arg per RL-4 exemption
    - RC-counting balance per arc.md sec-Non-Negotiable-Invariants
      invariant 1 (FipContract::Certified requires zero unmatched
      alloc/dealloc in realized IR)

  Soundness property:
    Forall v in owned_non_scalar_vars(F).
      RL-2 emits RcDec(v) at last_use(v) UNLESS last_use(v) is
      ownership-transferring;
      For every heap-allocating definition site of v, the realized
      IR contains a matching RcDec(v) on every CFG path from
      definition to function exit; RC count balanced per
      VF-4 / VF-6.

  Proof obligation:
    RC-counting induction over F's CFG (refinement engine):
      Refinement claim: pre-state has refcount = N at definition;
      post-state at function exit has refcount = N - decs_emitted;
      RL-2 ensures decs_emitted = N for v owned non-scalar with
      cardinality > 0 (not Absent).

    Case analysis on last_use(v) shape:
      Case last_use is non-transferring use (Apply Borrowed param,
                                              Project, IsShared,
                                              dbg, etc.):
        RL-2 emits RcDec(v) at the point;
        balance: +1 inc at definition, -1 dec at last use; net 0;
        refcount balanced.
      Case last_use is Return:
        Ownership-transferring; RL-2 SKIPS emission;
        caller receives v with owned reference; caller's RL-2
        owns the dec; balance maintained transitively.
      Case last_use is Construct/Reuse/CollectionReuse arg:
        Ownership-transferring; new aggregate captures v;
        v's refcount inherited by aggregate; RL-2 SKIPS emission;
        balance preserved.
      Case last_use is Set value:
        Ownership-transferring into the receiver's field;
        receiver inherits v's ref; RL-2 SKIPS; balance preserved.
      Case last_use is PartialApply capture:
        Ownership-transferring into closure environment;
        closure inherits v's ref; RL-2 SKIPS; balance preserved.
      Case last_use is Apply/Invoke to Owned param:
        Ownership-transferring into callee's parameter;
        callee's RL-2 owns the dec; balance preserved across the
        call boundary.
      Case last_use is Jump arg (RL-4 exemption):
        Block param IS successor's name; ownership transfers to
        successor block param; RL-2 SKIPS; successor block param's
        own RL-2 owns the dec; balance preserved.

    Refinement post-condition (per arc.md invariant 1):
      Every Construct/Reuse/CollectionReuse/PartialApply (allocations)
      paired with one RcDec on every reachable exit path;
      VF-4 FIP certification (sec-9 VF-4) verifies zero unmatched
      alloc/dealloc; RL-2 + RL-4 (edge-specific decs) +
      RL-5 (dead-at-entry cleanup) cover all owned-non-scalar
      cleanup obligations.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (alloc/dec balance per arc.md invariant 1)
      refinement (post-condition -> pre-condition implication on
                  every CFG path; pre: refcount = N; post: refcount
                  drops to 0 by function exit per matched decs)
      case_analysis (per-last-use-shape enumeration above —
                     ownership-transferring vs non-transferring)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: RL-shape scaffold-time; engine implementation pending
